'''Tann Gella''' was a [[Twi'lek]] [[Gender|female]] with a twin named [[Ann Gella]]. The pair were from the [[planet]] [[Ryloth]] and were [[Slavery|enslaved]], with the [[Podracer (profession)|podracer]] [[Sebulba]] purchasing Ann and Tann from the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]. In [[32 BBY]], Sebulba took part in the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] on the planet [[Tatooine]] and, prior to the race, Tann gave him a [[Yobana|massage]].

==Biography==
Tann Gella was an [[Rutian]] [[Twi'lek]] [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Force Collection" /> from the [[planet]] [[Ryloth]].<ref name="Geektionary French" /> She was the [[twin]] sister of [[Ann Gella]].<ref name="Force Collection" /> By [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of {{Film|I}} to [[32 BBY]].</ref> they had been [[Slavery|enslaved]] and were purchased as property by the [[Dug]] [[Podracer (profession)|podracer]] [[Sebulba]] from the [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]].<ref name="Force Collection" /> The Dug used the twins as yobanas and the pair caught the attention of other podracers like [[Mars Guo]] and [[Teemto Pagalies]].<ref name="DieWannaWanga">{{SW|url=news/die-wanna-wanga-encounters-of-the-twilek-kind|text=Die Wanna Wanga: Encounters of The Twi'lek Kind|nolive=1}}</ref> In that [[Standard year|year]], the twins were with Sebulba on the planet [[Tatooine]].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref>

The Dug planned to take part in the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]]<ref name="TPM" /> outside [[Mos Espa]] [[spaceport]],<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> and before the race began, the twins helped Sebulba prepare. While he sat with his [[Sebulba's Podracer|podracer]] in the [[Mos Espa Grand Arena]]'s [[hangar]], Tann massaged his shoulders while Ann<ref name="TPM" /> manicured<ref name="Geektionary" /> his toenails. The Dug enjoyed the ministrations of the Twi'leks and considered them comely,<ref name="DB">{{Databank|url=sebulba-biography-gallery|title=Sebulba Biography Gallery}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> although he was actually using the massage as a cover so he could guard his vehicle from race officials and other pilots.<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> 

==Personality and traits==
Tann was considered beautiful<ref name="DieWannaWanga" /> and had [[Color|blue]] skin and brown [[eye]]s.<ref name="Force Collection" /> 

==Equipment==
The twins wore matching yellow net [[Clothing|outfits]] with a gray headpiece and a silver collar while on Tatooine.<ref name="TPM" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Twilek_twins.jpg|thumb|right|250px|alt=Ann and Tann Gella stand together facing the viewer with the Mos Espa hangar visible behind them.|Ann and Tann Gella were played by real-life twins Nifa and Nishan Hindes.]]
Tann Gella was portrayed by actress [[Nishan Hindes]] in the film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']]<ref name="Blog">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-a-family-affair|text=''Star Wars'', A Family Affair|nolive=1}}</ref> which was released on [[May 19]], [[1999]].<ref name="Year by Year">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> Nishan acted alongside her real-life twin sister, [[Nifa Hindes]], who played Ann Gella.<ref name="Blog" /> Their scene was filmed on B Stage at [[Leavesden Studios]].<ref name="365Days">''[[Creating the Worlds of Star Wars: 365 Days]]''</ref>

Tann did not receive a name in the film<ref name="TPM" /> and was first identified in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] by the [[Star Wars video games|mobile card game]] ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'',<ref name="Force Collection" /> which initially launched in [[2013]]. Although the launch of ''Force Collection'' predates<ref name="Force Collection release">{{SW|url=news/announcing-star-wars-force-collection|text=Announcing Star Wars: Force Collection|nolive=1}}</ref> the ''Star Wars'' canon reset of [[2014]],<ref name="Legends">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Leland Chee]] confirmed that the game was kept updated to fit with canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|holocronkeeper|status/846807700482666496|[[Leland Chee]]|date=2017-03-28|quote=I'm not gonna go through the trouble of changing them and I don't have any reason to believe currently that anyone would. [&hellip;] On the off-chance that we DID have a current need to change any of these, we would have for Force Collection.|archivedate=20210505080831}} &mdash; [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] has confirmed that [[in-universe]] information from ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'' conforms with ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]].</ref> The [[Tann Gella/Legends|name]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first used in the ''[[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary]]'' reference book written by [[David West Reynolds (real person)|David West Reynolds]]<ref name="Visual Dictionary">''[[Star Wars: Episode I: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> and released on [[May 26]], 1999.<ref name="Amazon">{{CollectorCite|6|Books with Bite}}</ref>

